## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this for peak multi-tenant load?
- How would you ensure exactly-once processing given external sinks?
- How would you monitor latency and data-loss metrics effectively?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-preserving ML pipelines across tenants with governance constraints. It also probes how to coordinate training, model registry, and DR while controlling cost.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning across tenants
- Azure ML orchestration and Delta Lake
- Purview RBAC BYOK governance
- Drift monitoring and auditability
- DR and cost optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for federated training loop
function train_round(tenant_config, local_data_uri, model, aggregator_uri){
  const local_model = train(model, load(local_data_uri));
  const update = compute_update(local_model, model);
  send_update_to_server(aggregator_uri, update);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect and respond to drift across tenants?
- How would you handle non-IID data and stragglers in the federation?

## Why This Is Asked
The angle tests end-to-end design under regulatory constraints, real-time data flows, and cross-region DR.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time ingestion: MQTT → IoT Hub → Stream Analytics
- Consent governance and policy engine
- Data isolation: per-tenant Cosmos DB & Data Lake Gen2
- BYOK, Purview RBAC, GDPR/HIPAA readiness
- DR across paired EU regions; cost levers: reserved capacity, tiered storage

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPII(record) {
  if (!record) return record;
  const r = { ...record };
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = 'XXX-XX-XXXX';
  if (r.dob) r.dob = null;
  if (r.phone) r.phone = r.phone.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g, '*');
  return r;
}
```

